## Acceptance Criteria

### AC-1: Model Performance

- [ ] Primary metric meets or exceeds threshold on holdout test set
- [ ] Model outperforms documented baseline by minimum required margin
- [ ] No data leakage from target into feature set

### AC-2: Training Reproducibility

- [ ] Training pipeline produces identical results given the same seed and data
- [ ] Feature engineering steps are deterministic and documented
- [ ] All preprocessing transformations are fit on training data only

### AC-3: Deployment Readiness

- [ ] Model artifact is registered in the model registry
- [ ] Inference endpoint or batch job runs end-to-end without errors
- [ ] Predictions are logged for future monitoring and drift detection

### AC-4: Data Quality

- [ ] Feature distributions in serving data match training distribution (within tolerance)
- [ ] NULL handling for each feature follows documented fallback behavior
- [ ] No unseen categorical values crash inference

---

## Edge Cases and Constraints

| Scenario | Expected Behavior |
|----------|-------------------|
| Feature column is entirely NULL at inference | Use documented fallback value; log warning |
| Training data is too small (< {{ min_rows | default("1 000") }} rows) | Abort training; raise error with guidance |
| Class imbalance exceeds {{ imbalance_threshold | default("95/5") }} ratio | Apply oversampling or class weights; document choice |
| Model registry unavailable at deploy time | Fail fast with actionable error; do not serve stale model silently |
| Schema drift in feature source table | Fail inference with schema mismatch error; alert on-call |
| Retraining produces lower metric than current prod model | Block promotion; alert model owner for manual review |
